    "updated_at": "2019-10-20T17:53:07Z",
    "body": "@Calange, @Kwelity and I are trying to work out what workflows and expected behaviour different users use and what the expected behavior is for these workflows is, would it be possible for you to confirm yours. @caffeineflo and @ghg  you had similar issues in #550 can you add your workflows and expectations too?\r\n\r\n----\r\nMy own usage is as follows:\r\n\r\nI have a few [named profiles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-configure-profiles.html) setup and I will normally set the env var when I am doing some work on a particular account and the either unset the var after I am done or switch to a different account e.g\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nexport AWS_PROFILE=foo\r\naws ... \r\naws ...\r\nexport AWS_PROFILE=bar\r\n# or \r\nunset AWS_PROFILE\r\n```\r\n\r\nI follow a similar process with regions having a default region in the profile and I override it by exporting the `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` or `AWS_REGION` env vars depending on what I am doing.\r\n\r\nMy preference would be for starship to only display the aws module when one of the env vars is set.\r\nSo if the `AWS_PROFILE` env var is set I would like the aws module to display the profile name, I don't mind if it also displays the default region for that profile if it makes the module simpler, similar if the `AWS_REGION` env var is set I would like the aws module to display the region again I am ok with it showing `default` as the profile name if it makes the module simpler. If none of the env vars are set I would like the aws module to not display anything. \r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
