    "updated_at": "2019-10-22T09:04:08Z",
    "body": "Hello @andytom 🙂,\r\n\r\nI use a fish function to switch to my AWS profile: \r\n\r\n```bash\r\nfunction prod\r\nset -g -x AWS_PROFILE 'prod'\r\nend\r\n```\r\nWith this configuration it's ok but If I use the function with the variable AWS_DEFAULT_REGION:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nfunction prod\r\nset -g -x AWS_PROFILE 'prod'\r\nset -g -x AWS_DEFAULT_REGION 'eu-west-1'\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe default region is show in my prompt instead of the aws profile.\r\n\r\nFor the workflow, for me it's logical to see the profile only if the variable AWS_PROFILE is set and not to read the ~/.aws/config, but it's my point of view 🙂",
    "author_association": "NONE",
