    "updated_at": "2019-10-22T12:08:05Z",
    "body": "Hey there,\r\n\r\nto add to the conversation, I'll share my workflow, as well as the current behavior of the module (with my fix)\r\n\r\n### My workflow\r\nSo my workflow consist of dynamically loading and unloading my environment variables when I enter a directory (this is done via a shell plugin, `direnv`).\r\n\r\nSo every \"aws\" directory will have a .envrc that look like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nexport AWS_PROFILE=aws-prod\r\nexport AWS_REGION=us-east-2\r\n```\r\n\r\n### The current behavior\r\n\r\n\r\nNo environment variable:\r\n\r\n![starship_no_aws](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283071-4a19ea80-f4d3-11e9-8a2c-13bca43cc33e.png)\r\n\r\n`AWS_PROFILE=aws-prod`:\r\n\r\n![starship_aws_profile_set](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283204-7f263d00-f4d3-11e9-9540-2ac2e6336f08.png)\r\n\r\n`AWS_REGION=us-east-2`:\r\n\r\n![starship_aws_region_set](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283248-9d8c3880-f4d3-11e9-9ab2-5092498fd3e7.png)\r\n\r\n```\r\nAWS_PROFILE=aws-prod\r\nAWS_REGION=us-east-2\r\n```\r\n\r\n![starship_aws_profile_and_region_set](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283331-c6143280-f4d3-11e9-992c-b106fdb33e80.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\nAWS_PROFILE=aws-prod\r\nAWS_REGION=us-east-2\r\nAWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1\r\n```\r\n\r\n![starship_aws_profile_and_regions_set](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283397-e217d400-f4d3-11e9-965d-34cd17115fc8.png)\r\n\r\n`~/.aws/config`:\r\n```\r\n[profile aws-prod]\r\nregions=eu-west-7\r\n```\r\n\r\n![starship_aws_profile_set_from_conf](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283450-fa87ee80-f4d3-11e9-96b4-ca6cc7389a75.png)\r\n\r\n`~/.aws/config`:\r\n```\r\n[default]\r\nregions=eu-west-10\r\n```\r\n\r\n![starship_no_aws_with_default_conf](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2639732/67283596-45096b00-f4d4-11e9-9ea8-ba88d54d2453.png)\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is the default behavior, without setting `displayed_items` which allow to choose between \"region\", \"profile\" or both.\r\n\r\nMy only issue, is for the last one, it will show the default region in any directory. Except if you set `displayed_items = \"region\"` in the module config.",
